  FT["PH-H16590"] = {"id":"PH-H16590","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":9,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES STRENGTHENING THE FIGHT AGAINST ILLEGAL GAMBLING AND CLARIFYING THE JURISDICTION AND AUTHORITY OF CONCERNED AGENCIES IN THE REGULATION AND LICENSING OF GAMBLING AND ONLINE GAMING FACILITIES, AND FOR OTHER PURPOSES","orig":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES STRENGTHENING THE FIGHT AGAINST ILLEGAL GAMBLING AND CLARIFYING THE JURISDICTION AND AUTHORITY OF CONCERNED AGENCIES IN THE REGULATION AND LICENSING OF GAMBLING AND ONLINE GAMING FACILITIES, AND FOR OTHER PURPOSES"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 13","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 9 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00013_2017.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00013_2017.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H16590-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 1"},"text":{"en":"Law Enforcement and Government Agencies to Curb Illegal\nGambling. The Philippine National Police (PNP), the National Bureau of Investigation\n(NBI) and other law enforcement agencies are hereby ordered to intensify the fight\nagainst illegal gambling, in coordination with concerned agencies such as the\nDepartment of Justice (DOJ), Department of the Interior and Local Government (DILG),\nand the Department of Information and Communications Technology (DICT).\nThe same law enforcement agencies are further directed to coordinate and\npromptly act on requests of gambling regulatory authorities to investigate and put a stop\nto illegal gambling activities in their respective jurisdictions."}},{"id":"PH-H16590-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 2"},"text":{"en":"Illegal Gambling Defined. Pursuant to existing laws, \"illegal\ngambling\" is committed by any person who, in any manner, shall directly or indirectly\ntake part in any game scheme, regardless of whether winning thereat is dependent\nupon chance or skill or both, wherein wagers consisting of money, articles of value or\nrepresentative of value are at stake or made, when such game scheme is not\nauthorized or licensed by the government agency duly empowered by law or its charter\nto license or authorize the conduct of such games, or is conducted in a manner that\nviolates the terms and conditions duly prescribed by the said government agency.\nAll gambling activities, and activities and services directly or indirectly related to\nor in support of such gambling activities, conducted beyond the territorial jurisdiction of\nthe government authority which issued the license therefor, shall be dealt with as illegal"}},{"id":"PH-H16590-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 3"},"text":{"en":"Clarification on Online Gambling. No duly licensed online\ngambling operator, or provider of activities and services related to or in support of online\ngambling activities, shall directly or indirectly allow persons who are physically located\noutside the territorial jurisdiction of the licensing authority to place bets, or in any way\nparticipate, in the games conducted by such operator, whether through an online portal\nor similar means. Nothing herein, however, shall prohibit the duly licensed online\ngambling operator from allowing the participation of persons physically located outside\nPhilippine territory.\nThe license to operate online gambling granted to qualified operators shall not be\nassigned, shared, leased, transferred, sold or encumbered to any other party. Any\ngambling operator desiring to operate outside the jurisdiction of the government\n\nauthority wiich issued its existing license shall apply for a separate license with the\nappropriate authority."}},{"id":"PH-H16590-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 4"},"text":{"en":"Oversight Function. The Office of the President, through its duly\nauthorized representative, shall exercise oversight in the implementation of this Order.\nAs may be necessary, such representative shall, in coordination with relevant agencies,\nrecommend to the President the issuance of rules, regulations and directives for the\nsuppression of illegal gambling and the improvement of government efforts to raise\nrevenue from legitimate gambling activities.\nAll government agencies and authorities such as PAGCOR, CEZA, AFAB,\nAPECO, Bureau of Internal Revenue, Bureau of Immigration, Bureau of Customs, Anti-\nMoney Laundering Council, DILG, DICT, and Philippine Economic Zone Authority, are\nhereby directed to fully cooperate with and lend their assistance to the Office of the\nPresident or its duly authorized representative in the performance of the tasks and\nfunctions herein provided."}},{"id":"PH-H16590-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 5"},"text":{"en":"Reporting Requirement. PAGCOR, CEZA, AFAB, APECO and\nother similar regulatory entities, in coordination with the relevant law enforcement\nagencies, shall submit to the Office of the President, through the authorized\nrepresentative mentioned in Section 4 above, a consolidated report on the progress of\nthe fight against illegal gambling in their respective jurisdictions, within six (6) months\nfrom the effective date of this Order and every six (6) months thereafter."}},{"id":"PH-H16590-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 6"},"text":{"en":"Funding. The amounts necessary to carry out the provisions of\nthis Order shall be taken from available appropriations in the CY 2017 General\nAppropriations Act of the concerned agencies, subject to applicable budgetary rules and\nregulations. Thereafter, appropriations for the implementation of this Order shall be\nincorporated in the regular budget of the concerned agencies."}},{"id":"PH-H16590-A7","no":7,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 7"},"text":{"en":"Repeal. All executive orders, rules and regulations and other\nissuances or parts thereof which are inconsistent with this Executive Order, are hereby\nrevoked, amended, or modified accordingly."}},{"id":"PH-H16590-A8","no":8,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 8"},"text":{"en":"Separability. If any provision of this Executive Order is declared\ninvalid or unconstitutional, the other provisions not affected thereby shall remain valid\nand subsisting."}},{"id":"PH-H16590-A9","no":9,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 9"},"text":{"en":"Effectivity. This Executive Order shall take effect immediately\nupon its publication in a newspaper of general circulation.\nDONE, in the City of Manila, this 2nd day of February\nof Our Lord, Two Thousand and Seventeen.\nBy the President:\nSALVADOR C. MEDIALDEA\nExecutive Secretary\nARTIRED COPY:\nREPUBLIC OP THE\nPrILIPPINES\nMARIANITO M. DIMAANDAL\nDIRECTOR IV3 2 6-5 1\nMALACARANG RECORDS OFFICI"}}],"pack":"ph-p156"};
  FT["PH-H16591"] = {"id":"PH-H16591","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":5,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES MAINTAINING THE TEMPORARY MODIFICATION OF RATES OF IMPORT DUTY ON CERTAIN AGRICULTURAL PRODUCTS UNDER SECTION 1611 \"CUSTOMS MODERNIZATION AND TARIFF ACT","orig":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES MAINTAINING THE TEMPORARY MODIFICATION OF RATES OF IMPORT DUTY ON CERTAIN AGRICULTURAL PRODUCTS UNDER SECTION 1611 \"CUSTOMS MODERNIZATION AND TARIFF ACT"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 13","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 5 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00013_2023.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00013_2023.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H16591-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"en":"Rates of Import Duty. The articles specifically listed in Annex A hereof,\nas classified under Section 1611 of RA No. 10863, shall be subject to the MN rates of import\nduty in accordance with the schedule indicated opposite each article until 31 December\n2024.\nUpon the effectivity of this Order, all articles specifically listed in Annex A hereof,\nwhich are entered into or withdrawn from warehouses in the Philippines for consumption,\nshall be levied the MFN rates of duty as prescribed therein.\nThe rates of import duty on tariff headings and subheadings which are not listed in\nAnnex A hereof, and those listed but represented by the symbol \"XXX\" shall remain in full\nforce and effect."}},{"id":"PH-H16591-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"en":"Review. The MN tariff rates shall be subject to review after one (1) year\nof implementation of this Order. For this purpose, the NEDA shall submit to the President,\nthrough the Office of the Executive Secretary, its findings and recommendations on the"}},{"id":"PH-H16591-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3"},"text":{"en":"Separability. If any section or part of this Order is declared to be\nunconstitutional or invalid, the other sections or provisions not otherwise affected shall\nremain in full force and effect."}},{"id":"PH-H16591-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 4"},"text":{"en":"Repeal. All orders, rules, regulations, and issuances or parts thereof,\nwhich are inconsistent with this Order are hereby repealed or modified accordingly."}},{"id":"PH-H16591-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 5"},"text":{"en":"Effectivity. This Order shall take effect immediately after its complete\npublication in the Official Gazette or in a newspaper of general circulation.\nDONE, in the City of Manila, this 13th day of\nof Our Lord, Two Thousand and Twenty-Three.\nBy the President:\nOfice of the President\nMALACANANG RECORDS OFFICE\nATTY. CONCEPCION 73\nWE FERROLIND-ENAD\nLUCAS P. BEERSAMIN\nExecutive Secretary\n2\nREPUBLIC OF THE PHILIPPINES\n\n(1)\n02.07\n(2)\n0207.13.00.200\n0207.14\n0207.14.30.200\n0207.14.91\n0207.14.99.200\n0207.26.00.200\n0207 27\n0207.27.10.200\n0207.27.91\n0207.27.91.100\n0207.27.91.200\n0207.27.99.200\n0207.60.40.200\nDescription\n(3)\nMeat and edible offal, of the poultry of\nheading 01.05, fresh, chilled or frozen.\n- Of fowls of the species Gallus domesticus\n-- Cuts and offal, frozen:\n- - - - Mechanically deboned or separated\n- - Cuts and offal, frozen :\n- - Mechanically deboned or separated\nMFN Rate of Duty (%)\n2024\n2025\n(4)\n(5)\n5\n40\n30\n40"}}],"pack":"ph-p156"};
  FT["PH-H16592"] = {"id":"PH-H16592","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"LawPhil (HTML full text only)  |  https://lawphil.net/executive/execord/eo1936/eo_14_1936.html","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"Creating a \"Domestic Sugar Administration","orig":"Creating a \"Domestic Sugar Administration"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 14","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1936-01-21","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00014_1936_html.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00014_1936_html.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H16592-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE\nBY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES\n[ EXECUTIVE ORDER NO. 14, January 21, 1936 ]\nCREATING A “DOMESTIC SUGAR ADMINISTRATION”\nWHEREAS, under sections twelve and thirteen of Act Numbered Four thousand one hundred sixty-six,\nknown as “The Sugar Limitation Law,” the Governor-General of the Philippine Islands, and since the\ninauguration of the Commonwealth, the President of the Philippines, is authorized to issue rules and\nregulations governing the issuance of allotments and licenses and such other rules and regulations as he may\nconsider necessary for the carrying out of the purposes of said Act, and is moreover authorized to name and\nappoint such representatives or deputies as he may deem necessary to perform any of the duties and powers\ngranted to him therein, with such compensation and emoluments as may be fixed by him;\nWHEREAS,the President of the United States on October nineteenth, nineteen hundred and thirty-five,\nreturned to the Secretary of Agriculture of the United States, approved, a letter to him from the latter, dated\nOctober fourteenth, nineteen hundred and thirty-five, which reads in part as follows:\n“Accordingly, I respectfully request that pursuant to section 7, paragraph 4, of the Tydings-McDuffie Act\n(Philippine Independence Act), you delegate to the High Commissioner of the Philippine Islands the authority\nto perform the additional duty of making allotments, in my name, of the quota of sugar for the calendar year\n1936”;"}}],"pack":"ph-p156"};
  FT["PH-H16593"] = {"id":"PH-H16593","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"LawPhil (HTML full text only)  |  https://lawphil.net/executive/execord/eo1944/eo_14-w_1944.html","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"W  Creating the Currency Committee","orig":"W  Creating the Currency Committee"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 14","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1944-06-20","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00014_1944_html.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00014_1944_html.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H16593-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE\nBY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES\n[ EXECUTIVE ORDER NO. 14-W, June 20, 1944 ]\nCREATING THE CURRENCY COMMITTEE\nWHEREAS, the indiscriminate issue of paper currency in the Philippines by the enemy has caused\nconsiderable confusion and chaos in the monetary system, resulting in the disappearance from the circulation\nof the economic condition of the inhabitants of the country;\nNOW THEREFORE I, MANUEL L. QUEZON, President of the Philippines, by virtue of the powers vested\nin me by law, do hereby create a Currency Committee which shall confer with the representatives of the\nDepartment of the Interior, of State, of War, and of the Treasury of the United States Government with the\nview to remedying the monetary situation in the Philippines and to arrange for the printing of new Philippine\nTreasury Certificates and the immediate minting of subsidiary coins ready for use upon the landing of the\nliberating forces on Philippine soil.\nThis Committee will act under the supervision of, and be directly responsible to, the President of the\nPhilippines.\nDone at the City of Saranac Lake, State of New York, United States of America, this twentieth day of June, in\nthe year of Our Lord, nineteen hundred and forty-four, and of the Commonwealth of the Philippines, the ninth.\nMANUEL L. QUEZON\nPresident of the Philippines"}}],"pack":"ph-p156"};
  FT["PH-H16594"] = {"id":"PH-H16594","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACAIANG RESIDENCE CP THE PRESIDENT OP TUD PHTLIPPINES BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPFINES DXECUTIVE CRDER 10. 14 CRATING A PRELIMINARY COMMITTED FOR THE REVISION OF THE REVISED ADMINISTRATIVE CODE.","orig":"MALACAIANG RESIDENCE CP THE PRESIDENT OP TUD PHTLIPPINES BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPFINES DXECUTIVE CRDER 10. 14 CRATING A PRELIMINARY COMMITTED FOR THE REVISION OF THE REVISED ADMINISTRATIVE CODE."},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 14","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00014_1966.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00014_1966.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H16594-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"...\n25\nA Ropresentativo from the Mouse\nof Representatives, to be\ndosignated by the Speaker . . . Member\nA Represontativo or Local Govern-\nThe U.P. Law Center shall act as tho Secreta-\nriat. The Head of the UP. Division of Research\nand Law Reforms shall be the Project Director.\nshall direct the administrative functions of tho\nCommittee and oxercise overall supervision ovor the\nporsonnel of the project.\nThe Committee is empowered to call upon any\ndepartment, bureau, office, , subdivision,_ agency\nor instrumentality of the governmont including go-\nvernment-owned or controlled corporations, for such\nassistance as it may need in the porformanco of its\nThe Project Director is authorised to grant\nto the boreonnel of tho project honorariums or\nallowances in Such reasonable anounts as he may\nThe Committee shall finish its work and sub-\nmit to the President of the Philippines its report,\ntogother with the draft of a now Aáministrative\nCode for submission to tho Concross of the Phi-\nlippines, , not later than December 31, 1966.\nBone in the City of Manila, this 24th day of\nFebruary, in the year of Our Lord, nineteen hundred\nand sixty-six.\n(SGD.) FERDINAND D. MARCOS\nFresident of the Philippines\nBy the Prosident:\n(SGD.) RATAEL M. GALAS\nExecutivo Secretary\n26"}}],"pack":"ph-p156"};
  FT["PH-H16595"] = {"id":"PH-H16595","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"LawPhil (source has HTML full text only)","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":5,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"A  Amending Executive Order No. 14","orig":"A  Amending Executive Order No. 14"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 14","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1986-08-18","completenessNote":"全文，共 5 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00014_1986_html.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00014_1986_html.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H16595-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Sec 1"},"text":{"en":"Section 3 of Executive Order No. 14 dated May 7, 1986 is hereby amended to read as follows:\n\"Sec. 3. The civil suits to recover unlawfully acquired property under Republic Act No. 1379 or for\nrestitution, reparation of damages, or indemnification for consequential and other damages or any other civil\nactions under the Civil Code or other existing laws filed with the Sandiganbayan against Ferdinand E. Marcos,\nImelda R. Marcos, members of their immediate family, close relatives, subordinates, close and/or business\nassociates, dummies, agents and nominees, may proceed independently of any criminal proceedings and may\nbe proved by a preponderance of evidence.\""}},{"id":"PH-H16595-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Sec 2"},"text":{"en":"Section 4 of Executive Order No. 14 dated May 7, 1986 is hereby amended to read as follows:\n\"Sec. 4. A witness may refuse on the basis of his privilege against self-incrimination, to testify or provide\nother information in proceeding before the Sandiganbayan if the witness believes that such testimony or\nprovision of information would tend to incriminate him or subject him to prosecution. Upon such refusal the\nSandiganbayan may order the witness to testify or provide information.\nThe witness may refuse to comply with the order on the basis of his privilege against self-incrimination; but\nno testimony or other information compelled under the order (or any information directly or indirectly derived\nfrom such testimony, or other information) may be used against the witness in any criminal case, except a\nprosecution for perjury, giving a false statement, or otherwise failing to comply with the order.\""}},{"id":"PH-H16595-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Sec 3"},"text":{"en":"Section 5 of dated Executive Order No. 14 May 7, 1986 is hereby amended to read as follows:\n\"Sec. 5. The Presidential Commission on Good Government is authorized to grant immunity from criminal\nprosecution to any person who provides information or testifies in any investigation conducted by such\nCommission to establish the unlawful manner in which any respondent, defendant or accused has acquired or\naccumulated the property or properties in question in any case where such information or testimony is\nnecessary to ascertain or prove the latter's guilt or his civil liability. The immunity thereby granted shall be\ncontinued to protect the witness who repeats such testimony before the Sandiganbayan when required to do so\nby the latter or by the Commission.\""}},{"id":"PH-H16595-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Sec 4"},"text":{"en":"Section 7 Executive Order No. 14 dated May 7, 1986 is hereby amended as follows:\n\"Sec. 7. The provisions of this Executive Order shall prevail over any laws or parts thereof, or the Rules of\nCourt as regards the investigation, prosecution, and trial of cases to recover the ill-gotten wealth accumulated\nby the persons mentioned in Executive Orders Nos. 1 and 2.\""}},{"id":"PH-H16595-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"Sec 5"},"text":{"en":"This Executive Order shall take effect immediately.\nDone in the City of Manila, Philippines, this 18th day of August, in the year of Our Lord, nineteen hundred\nand eighty-six."}}],"pack":"ph-p156"};
  FT["PH-H16596"] = {"id":"PH-H16596","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"PMS LIBRARY OF THE PHiliPPINES","orig":"PMS LIBRARY OF THE PHiliPPINES"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 14","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00014_1992.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00014_1992.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H16596-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"assistance\nfor regular\nmedication and the acquisition\naids and appliances;\nWHEREAS, SSS permanent\ndisability\npensioners,\nnot entitled\nto a monthly supplemental\nmust likewise\nfinancially\nin the additional\nexpenses similar to those of SSS\ndisability\npensioners;\nWHEREAS, actuarial\nshow that the SSS and EC funds can\nfinance a 10% across-the-board\npension increase to all SSS\nand EC pensioners\nas of August\n31, 1992, and a supplemental\nof P300 a month for SSS permanent\ndisability\npensioners\nout impairing\nthe viability\nof both funds\nnor necessitating\nan increase\nin the rates of contribution;\nNOW, THEREFORE,\nI, FIDEL V. RAMOS, President\nPhilippines,\nof the powers vested\nin me by law, do hereby\nThe monthly\npension of the surviving\npensioners\nas of August\n31, 1992 shall be increased\nby ten per cent\n(10%) .\nThe permanent\ndisability\npensioners\n555 shall be entitled\nto a monthly supplemental\npension of three\n2/\n3.\n1,\n1992.\nthe year of our Lord,\nnineteen hundred\nand ninety-two.\n-\nBy the Presiden~:-\n~"}}],"pack":"ph-p156"};
  FT["PH-H16597"] = {"id":"PH-H16597","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":5,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MAIJACANAN BY THE PRESIPENT OF THE PHILIPPINES EXECUTIVE ORDER NO.","orig":"MAIJACANAN BY THE PRESIPENT OF THE PHILIPPINES EXECUTIVE ORDER NO."},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 14","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 5 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00014_1998.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00014_1998.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H16597-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 4"},"text":{"en":"Honoraria\nand Allowances.\nThe Commission\nfor honoraria\nand allowances\nfor council\nmembers and its\npersonnel subject to existing rules and regulations."}},{"id":"PH-H16597-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 5"},"text":{"en":"Chairman\nand Vice Chairman\nof the Commission.\nshall preside over the meetings of the Commission and shall\nits decisions.\nHe shall exercise over-all supervision\ncontrol on the operations and programs of the Commission.\nThe Commission\nelect from among its members a vice\nchairman who shall act as chairman in case the chairman is unable to\ntemporarily\nperform his functions\nor in case of vacancy in the Office of\nthe Chairman.\nHe shall perform such other functions\nassigned to him by the chairman.\nand Administrative\nStaff. The Commission\nshall organize its technical and administrative\nstaff under the secretariat\nto be headed by an executive director who shall be designated by the\nThe executive director shall have at least five (5) years\nrelevant experience in technical and administrative\nhold office on a full time basis and shall not be removed except for cause.\nThe technical\nand administrative\nstaff shall be composed of personnel\nalso to be designated by the chairman.\nThe shall receive such salary and\nremuneration\nas may be determined\nby the Commission\nexisting rules and regulations.\n4\n\nTerm of the Commission.\nThe Commission shall cease\nto exist on June 30, 2000 unless its term is extended by an act of\nCongress or by the President.\n8.\nRegulations.\nCommission\npromulgate the rules and regulations to implement the provisions of this\nExecutive Order. Such rules and regulations shall take effect fifteen (15)\ndays after their publication in a newspaper of general circulation."}},{"id":"PH-H16597-A9","no":9,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 9"},"text":{"en":"Separability\nIn the event that the provisions of\nthis Executive Order are hereby declared to be separable and in the event\nany provisions\nor part thereof is declared unconstitutional\nprovisions or parts thereof which are not affected there by shall remain in\nfull force and effect."}},{"id":"PH-H16597-A10","no":10,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 10"},"text":{"en":"Repealing\nClause. All laws, decrees, executive orders,\nadministrative\norders, rules and regulations\ninconsistent\nherewith are\nhereby repealed, amended or modified accordingly."}},{"id":"PH-H16597-A11","no":11,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 11"},"text":{"en":"EFFECTIVITY.\nThis Executive Order shall take effectimme\nDONE in the City of Manila, Philippines,\nthis19.!;.l}..day of Au g us t inthe\nyear of Our Lord, Nineteen Hundred\nand Ninety-Eight.\n,\nBy the President:\nRONALDa B. ZAMORA"}}],"pack":"ph-p156"};
  FT["PH-H16598"] = {"id":"PH-H16598","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":2,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACAÑANd PMS LIBRARY CREATION OF 'THE CABINET CLUSTER FOR SOCIALLY EQUITABLE AGRICULTURAL MODERNIZATION","orig":"MALACAÑANd PMS LIBRARY CREATION OF 'THE CABINET CLUSTER FOR SOCIALLY EQUITABLE AGRICULTURAL MODERNIZATION"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 14","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 2 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00014_2001.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00014_2001.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H16598-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 1"},"text":{"en":"Functions of Cluster ^\nCluster A shall have the following functions:\n1. To serve as the venue for the formulation, review and recommendations of policies\nthat should provide the enabling environment for the attainment of the goals of\nagricultural modernization founded on social equity.\n2. To work as a team thereby ensuring that common policy direction towards socially\nequitable agricultural modernization is adhered in the respective programs of delivery\nof support services.\n3. To rationalize the use of respective resources towards a convergence program that\nshould ensure a sustainable and equitable modernization process."}},{"id":"PH-H16598-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 2"},"text":{"en":"Effectivity. This Executive Order shall take effect immediately.\nDONE in the City of Manila, this 7th day of May in the year of Our Lord, Two\nThousand and One.\nBy the President:\nRENATO C. CORONA\nPresidential Chic of Start\nPRIS LIBRARY,\nPOMA Outgoing # 02234\nPMS LIBRARY BCODE001983"}}],"pack":"ph-p156"};
  FT["PH-H16599"] = {"id":"PH-H16599","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":3,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"AAALACANAN PALACE, BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES TRANSFERRING THE CONTROL AND SUPERVISION OF THE PHILIPPINE CHARITY SWEEPSTAKES OFFICE FROM THE DEPARTMENT OF (DOH) TO THE OFFICE OF THE PRESIDENT","orig":"AAALACANAN PALACE, BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES TRANSFERRING THE CONTROL AND SUPERVISION OF THE PHILIPPINE CHARITY SWEEPSTAKES OFFICE FROM THE DEPARTMENT OF (DOH) TO THE OFFICE OF THE PRESIDENT"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 14","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 3 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00014_2010.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00014_2010.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H16599-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 1"},"text":{"en":"The direct control and supervision\nover the Philippine\nCharity Sweepstakes Office shall hereby be transferred\nfrom the Department of\nHealth to the Office of the President"}},{"id":"PH-H16599-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 2"},"text":{"en":"All orders, issuances,\nrules and regulations\nor parls thereof\ninconsistent with this Executive Order are herebv repealed or modified\naccordingly."}},{"id":"PH-H16599-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 3"},"text":{"en":"This Executive\nOrder shall take effect immediatelv\nDONE in the City of Manila, this'trgdday\noflbrurbein the Year of Our Lord,\nTwo Thousand and Ten.\nof $e $reeiberu\nolge Slrlippirer\nilil ilil lt il|il\nilil il|| iliil\nhxAlilfltilTfi\nDate uploaded: November 24, 2010\nPCDSPO Official Gazette"}}],"pack":"ph-p156"};
  FT["PH-H16600"] = {"id":"PH-H16600","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":11,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES INTERNATIONAL CORPORATION AS A SUBSIDIARY OF THE BASES CONVERSION AND DEVELOPMENT AUTHORITY, AND MAINTAINING THE POLICY SUPERVISION AND OPERATIONAL CONTROL OF THE DEPARTMENT OF TRANSPORTATION OVER THE CLARK INTERNATIONAL AIRPORT","orig":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES INTERNATIONAL CORPORATION AS A SUBSIDIARY OF THE BASES CONVERSION AND DEVELOPMENT AUTHORITY, AND MAINTAINING THE POLICY SUPERVISION AND OPERATIONAL CONTROL OF THE DEPARTMENT OF TRANSPORTATION OVER THE CLARK INTERNATIONAL AIRPORT"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 14","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 11 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00014_2017.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00014_2017.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H16600-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 1"},"text":{"en":"Declaration of Policy. There is a need to facilitate the full\ndevelopment of the Clark International Airport (the Airport) as a major and alternative\ngateway to and from the Philippines to achieve economic efficiency and support the\ndevelopment thrust of the government."}},{"id":"PH-H16600-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 2"},"text":{"en":"Restructuring of CIAC. The CIAC is hereby restructured from\nbeing an attached agency of DOT to a subsidiary of BCDA. The ownership of CIAC\nshall be transferred to BCDA.\nThe DOT is hereby ordered to facilitate the transfer and convevance of the\nshares currently owned by the Republic of the Philippines, as well as those shares\nheld in the name of its nominee stockholders, in favor of BCD and its nominees;\nProvided, however, that any delay in the execution of such documents of transfer\nand conveyance of the shares of stock of CIAC shall not, in any event, delay, hinder\nor deter the immediate exercise of ownership rights over CIAC by BCDA.\nThe respective governing boards and management of ClAC and BCDA are\ndirected to implement all pertinent laws, rules and regulations necessary for the said\n\ntransfer of shares, and to take all proper and necessary steps under Securities and\nExchange Commission regulations to accomplish this purpose.\nAll other heads of government departments, bureaus, offices, agencies,\ngovernment-owned and -controlled corporations and instrumentalities are hereby\nenjoined to render full assistance and cooperation to CIAC for the full development"}},{"id":"PH-H16600-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 3"},"text":{"en":"Mandate of CIAC. The CIAC shall only engage in civil aviation,\naviation-related services and aviation-related logistics activities within CCAC and the\nClark Industrial Estate 5 areas, as defined in EO No. 716. For all other business\nactivities, prior approval of the DOT and BCDA shall be secured."}},{"id":"PH-H16600-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 4"},"text":{"en":"Authority of DOT. The DOT shall exercise policy supervision\nand full regulatory and operational control over the operations of the Airport."}},{"id":"PH-H16600-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 5"},"text":{"en":"Board of Directors. The powers and functions of the CIAC shall\nbe vested in and exercised by a Board of Directors to be composed of the following:\nChairperson:\nSecretary of Transportation\nor designated representative (ex officio)\nVice-Chairpersons:\nSecretary of Tourism\nor designated representative (ex officio)\nPresident of the BCDA\nor designated representative (ex officio)\nPresident and Chief Executive Officer of the CIAC\nor designated representative (ex officio)\nThe Director General of the Civil Aviation Authority\nof the Philippines (CAAP) or designated\nrepresentative (ex officio), and six (6) other\nmembers to be appointed by the President of the\nPhilippines, upon consultation with the Secretary\nof Transportation and President of the BCDA;\nProvided, however, that the nomination and\nappointment of the six (6) appointive directors shall\ncomply with the provisions of RA 10149, otherwise\nknown as the \"GOCC Governance Act of 2011.\""}},{"id":"PH-H16600-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 6"},"text":{"en":"Authority of CDC. CDC shall continue to exercise its authority\nas the implementing arm of the BCD within the CFZ and CSEZ, pursuant to Section\n15 of RA No. 7227, as amended by RA No. 9400."}},{"id":"PH-H16600-A7","no":7,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 7"},"text":{"en":"Recognition of Existing Contracts. All contracts, leases and\nbusiness arrangements previously entered into by CDC within the CCAC shall be\nhonored, subject to applicable laws and issuances, including the terms and\n\nconditions that may be stipulated in the implementing rules and regulations of this"}},{"id":"PH-H16600-A8","no":8,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 8"},"text":{"en":"Implementing Rules and Regulations. The BCDA, CDC and\nCIAC, in consultation with DOT, are hereby directed to adopt implementing rules\nand regulations within thirty (30 days from the effectivity of this Order."}},{"id":"PH-H16600-A9","no":9,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 9"},"text":{"en":"Repeal. All orders, proclamations, rules, regulations, or parts\nthereof, which are inconsistent with any of the provisions of this Order are hereby\nrepealed or modified accordingly."}},{"id":"PH-H16600-A10","no":10,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 10"},"text":{"en":"Separability. If any provision of this Order be declared invalid\nor unconstitutional, the other provisions unaffected shall remain valid and subsisting."}},{"id":"PH-H16600-A11","no":11,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 11"},"text":{"en":"Effectivity. This Order shall take effect immediately upon\npublication in a newspaper of general circulation.\nDONE, in the City of Manila, this 28th day of February\nthe year of our Lord Two Thousand and Seventeen.\nBy the President:\nSALVADOR C. MEDIALDEA\nExecutive Secretary\nCERTIFIED COPY.\nREPUBLIC OF THE PHILIPPINES\n5 3-1-7577\nMARIANITO M. DIMAANDAL\nDIRECTOR IV\n887\nMALACARANG RECORDS OFFICI:"}}],"pack":"ph-p156"};
  FT["PH-H16601"] = {"id":"PH-H16601","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":9,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES APPROVING AND ADOPTING THE PHILIPPINE DEVELOPMENT PLAN FOR THE PERIOD 2023-2028","orig":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES APPROVING AND ADOPTING THE PHILIPPINE DEVELOPMENT PLAN FOR THE PERIOD 2023-2028"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 14","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 9 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00014_2023.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00014_2023.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H16601-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"en":"Adoption, Dissemination, and Implementation of the PDP 2023-\n2028. All national government agencies, government-owned or -controlled\ncorporations (GOCCs), government financial institutions (GFI), other national\ngovernment offices and instrumentalities, government corporate entities (CEs), state\nuniversities and colleges (SUCs), and local government units (LGUs), whether or not\nthey receive funding support through the General Appropriations Act (GAA), are\nhereby directed to adopt and disseminate the PDP 2023-2028 and undertake efforts\nleading to its full implementation."}},{"id":"PH-H16601-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"en":"Alignment of Agency Programs and Projects with the PDP\n2023-2028. All national government agencies, GOCCs, GFIs, other national\ngovernment offices and instrumentalities, GCEs, SUCs, and LGUs are hereby directed\nto align their budgetary and departmental/corporate programs with the strategies and\nactivities identified in the PDP 2023-2028."}},{"id":"PH-H16601-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3"},"text":{"en":"The PIP 2023-2028. In the submission of their priority programs and\nprojects, all heads of national government agencies, GOCCs, GFIs, other national\ngovernment offices and instrumentalities, GCEs, and SUCs are hereby instructed to\nadhere to the 07 October 2022 PIP Formulation Guidelines issued by the NEDA.\nThe formulation of the PIP 2023-2028 shall be completed by the first quarter of\n2023 and updated annually or when deemed necessary by the NEDA."}},{"id":"PH-H16601-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 4"},"text":{"en":"PDP and PIP Monitoring and Reporting. The NEDA Secretariat\nshall work together with various implementing agencies for the prioritization and\nsequencing of identified strategies, policies, programs, and projects, including\nproposed legislation. The monitoring of outcomes and implementation shall be\nreported regularly to the appropriate NEDA Board Inter-Agency Committees (IACs),\nCabinet Sectors, and other existing IACs of the government.\nAll national government agencies, GOCCs, GFIs, other national government\noffices and instrumentalities, GCEs, and SUCs, are hereby directed to submit to the\nBoard, through the\nSecretariat, the agency\nperformance/accomplishment reports with respect to the outcomes and outputs\nidentified in the PDP and PIP, in the format and frequency prescribed by the NEDA\nSecretariat. The NEDA Secretariat shall prepare the Socioeconomic Report to present\nthe accomplishments of outputs and outcomes and recommend policy directions\nmoving forward.\n2"}},{"id":"PH-H16601-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 5"},"text":{"en":"Additional Issuances. The NEDA Secretary is hereby authorized\nto issue such memoranda, circulars, or other orders as may be considered necessary\nor advisable in the coordination of the implementation, monitoring, assessment, and\nupdating of the PDP and PIP."}},{"id":"PH-H16601-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 6"},"text":{"en":"Funding. The Department of Budget and Management shall provide\nthe necessary budgetary support for the implementation, monitoring, assessment, and\nupdating of the PDP and PIP. The appropriations necessary for the continued\nimplementation of this Order for the succeeding ears shall be prepared in accordance\nwith regular government budget procedures and shall be included in the budget of the\nconcerned departments, agencies, and instrumentalities of the national government,\nunder the annual GAA."}},{"id":"PH-H16601-A7","no":7,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 7"},"text":{"en":"Separability. If any section or part of this Order is declared to be\nunconstitutional or invalid, the other sections or provisions not otherwise affected shall\nremain in full force and effect."}},{"id":"PH-H16601-A8","no":8,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 8"},"text":{"en":"Repeal. All other orders, guidelines, rules, regulations, and\nissuances or parts thereof, which are inconsistent with the provisions of this Order are\nhereby repealed or modified accordingly."}},{"id":"PH-H16601-A9","no":9,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 9"},"text":{"en":"Effectivity. This Order shall take effect immediately.\nDONE, in the City of Manila, this 27th day of January, in the year of Our\nLord, Two Thousand and Twenty-Three.\nBy the President:\n(\nLUCASP. BERSAMIN\nExecutive Secretary\nOffice of the President\nMALACAÑANG RECORDS OFFICE\nATTY, CONCEPCION ZEM E: FERROLINO-ENAD\n44. 130 hA3 DIRECTOR IN\n3\nREPUBLIC OF THE PHILIPPINES"}}],"pack":"ph-p156"};
  FT["PH-H16602"] = {"id":"PH-H16602","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"LawPhil (HTML full text only)  |  https://lawphil.net/executive/execord/eo1936/eo_15_1936.html","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"Abolishing the Barrio of Cawa-Cawa, Municipality of Zamboanga, Province of Zamboanga, and Organizing the Sitio of Punta Gabilan, Said Municipality, Into An Independent Barrio Under the Name of Punta Gabilan.","orig":"Abolishing the Barrio of Cawa-Cawa, Municipality of Zamboanga, Province of Zamboanga, and Organizing the Sitio of Punta Gabilan, Said Municipality, Into An Independent Barrio Under the Name of Punta Gabilan."},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 15","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1936-02-03","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00015_1936_html.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00015_1936_html.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H16602-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE\nBY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES\n[ EXECUTIVE ORDER NO. 15, February 03, 1936 ]\nABOLISHING THE BARRIO OF CAWA-CAWA, MUNICIPALITY OF ZAMBOANGA, PROVINCE OF\nZAMBOANGA, AND ORGANIZING THE SITIO OF PUNTA GABILAN, SAID MUNICIPALITY, INTO\nAN INDEPENDENT BARRIO UNDER THE NAME OF PUNTA GABILAN\nUpon petition of the municipal council of Zamboanga, Zamboanga, and recommendation of the provincial\nboard of said province, concurred in by the Director of the Bureau of non-Christian Tribes and the Secretary\nof the Interior, and pursuant to the provisions of section sixty-eight of the Revised Administrative Code, the\nBarrio of Cawa-Cawa, Municipality of Zamboanga, Province of Zamboanga, is hereby abolished, and the sitio\nof Punta Gabilan in said municipality, together with the territory comprising the barrio herein abolished, is\nhereby organized into an independent barrio under the name of Punta Gabilan.\nThe changes herein made shall take effect on March first, nineteen hundred and thirty-six.\nDone at the City of Manila, this third day of February, in the year of Our Lord, nineteen hundred and\nthirty-six, and of the Commonwealth of the Philippines, the first.\nMANUEL L. QUEZON\nPresident of the Philippines\nBy the President:\nTEOFILO SISON\nSecretary of the Interior"}}],"pack":"ph-p156"};
  FT["PH-H16603"] = {"id":"PH-H16603","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACAÑ ANG RESIDENCE OF THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES OTHERWISE KNOWN AS THE CASSAVA FLOUR LAW, IN THE INTEREST OF THE NATIONAL ECONOMY.","orig":"MALACAÑ ANG RESIDENCE OF THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES OTHERWISE KNOWN AS THE CASSAVA FLOUR LAW, IN THE INTEREST OF THE NATIONAL ECONOMY."},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 15","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00015_1954.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00015_1954.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H16603-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"caasava flour as set forth in the rules and regulations which\nmay be prescribed by the PRISCO.\n2. For the purpose of implementing the provisions of this\nOrder, the PRISCO is hereby authorized to collect a service fee\nof one-half of one per centum (1/2%) of the face value of the\ncassava flour for which it makes the required certification to\nthe Central Bank of the Philippines, the said fee to be used to\ndefray the expenses of certification, regulation and supervision.\nNo other fee shall be imposed.\nAny unexpended balance thereof\nshall be spent by the PRISCO for surveys and researches, promotion\nand publicity, and general development of the cassava industry.\n3. In order to Insure that a fair and equitable percentage\nof dollar allocations granted to wheat flour importers, said list\nto be held by the PRISCO as confidential information which shall\nnot be released to the public or to individual Importers.\n4. Any Importer of wheat flour who refuses or purposely avoids\nor deliherately fails to comply with the conditions laid down In\nparagraph 1 hereof shall be subject to the penalties provided in\nRepublic Act No. 657.\n5. All executive orders, administrative orders and proclama-\ntions, or parts thereof, inconsistent herewith are hereby repealed\nor modified accordingly.\nDone in the City of Manila, this 15th day of February, in\nthe year of Our Lord, nineteen hundred and fifty-four, and of\nthe Independence of the Philippines, the eighth.\n(SGD.) RAMON MAGSAYSAY\nPresident of the Philippines\nBy the President:\n(SGD.) FRED RUIZ CASTRO\nExecutive Secretary"}}],"pack":"ph-p156"};
